1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:02,630
Every dead sign on this
street is a warning.

2
00:00:02,630 --> 00:00:04,370
Tonight, one of them is for me.

3
00:00:05,167 --> 00:00:07,347
Something is
sending me messages.

4
00:00:07,347 --> 00:00:08,177
In neon.

5
00:00:08,087 --> 00:00:09,697
Not me. I only do insults.

6
00:00:09,637 --> 00:00:10,197
I'm Mara.

7
00:00:10,197 --> 00:00:11,557
I fix signs, at night.

8
00:00:11,557 --> 00:00:12,237
That's Zip.

9
00:00:12,237 --> 00:00:13,347
He complains.

10
00:00:13,207 --> 00:00:14,387
I supervise.

11
00:00:14,507 --> 00:00:16,847
Tonight's job was
left on the step.

12
00:00:16,847 --> 00:00:17,387
No name.

13
00:00:17,387 --> 00:00:18,227
No note.

14
00:00:18,207 --> 00:00:20,867
Just my mother's mark,
scratched on the back.

15
00:00:21,057 --> 00:00:22,887
Mara, she's been
gone nine years.

16
00:00:22,937 --> 00:00:24,607
I know how long it's been.

17
00:00:24,857 --> 00:00:26,267
So I woke it up.

18
00:00:27,237 --> 00:00:28,537
It says hello! It's friendly.

19
00:00:28,537 --> 00:00:29,287
I love it.

20
00:00:29,617 --> 00:00:30,807
That is not hello.

21
00:00:30,797 --> 00:00:32,487
Help. Zip, pull the plug.

22
00:00:32,467 --> 00:00:33,817
It was never plugged in.

23
00:00:34,147 --> 00:00:35,807
Then it lit one more word.

24
00:00:36,007 --> 00:00:36,697
Tomorrow, what?

25
00:00:36,697 --> 00:00:37,957
Finish your sentence!

26
00:00:38,077 --> 00:00:40,947
And outside, a sign I
never made switched on.

27
00:00:41,277 --> 00:00:42,597
It had my name.

28
00:00:43,227 --> 00:00:45,237
And someone was
waiting under it.

29
00:00:46,033 --> 00:00:48,053
I asked a dead
sign where it was.

30
00:00:48,053 --> 00:00:49,093
It answered.

31
00:00:49,143 --> 00:00:49,393
Nine.

32
00:00:49,393 --> 00:00:49,893
Nine what?

33
00:00:49,893 --> 00:00:50,193
Lives?

34
00:00:50,193 --> 00:00:51,353
I'm down to four.

35
00:00:51,263 --> 00:00:51,943
Number nine.

36
00:00:51,943 --> 00:00:53,693
But this street stops at seven.

37
00:00:53,693 --> 00:00:54,553
That's us.

38
00:00:54,463 --> 00:00:56,103
Great. It's lying. Bedtime.

39
00:00:56,433 --> 00:00:58,403
Working late, Miss Reyes?

40
00:00:58,313 --> 00:00:59,113
Mister Crane.

41
00:00:59,113 --> 00:01:01,393
The rent isn't due until Friday.

42
00:01:01,333 --> 00:01:02,983
Oh, I'm not here for rent.

43
00:01:02,983 --> 00:01:04,063
I saw your light.

44
00:01:04,063 --> 00:01:06,203
Your mother worked late, too.

45
00:01:06,253 --> 00:01:08,043
What do you know
about my mother?

46
00:01:07,983 --> 00:01:10,923
Only that she would not
stop asking questions.

47
00:01:10,923 --> 00:01:11,933
Sleep well.

48
00:01:12,253 --> 00:01:12,813
I hate him.

49
00:01:12,813 --> 00:01:14,483
He smells like burnt toast.

50
00:01:14,533 --> 00:01:16,673
He walked off, to
where the street ends.

51
00:01:16,673 --> 00:01:18,203
And he never came back.

52
00:01:18,263 --> 00:01:19,613
So we went to look.

53
00:01:19,873 --> 00:01:21,943
That wall did not
have a door yesterday.

54
00:01:22,063 --> 00:01:23,273
It was nailed shut.

55
00:01:23,273 --> 00:01:24,593
From the inside.

56
00:01:24,703 --> 00:01:26,463
Then please, please
do not knock.

57
00:01:26,513 --> 00:01:27,583
I knocked.

58
00:01:30,193 --> 00:01:31,693
I would like to go home now.

59
00:01:32,483 --> 00:01:34,283
Number nine doesn't exist.

60
00:01:34,283 --> 00:01:35,823
So why is it open?

61
00:01:35,693 --> 00:01:36,423
Great question.

62
00:01:36,423 --> 00:01:37,743
Let's never find out.

63
00:01:37,653 --> 00:01:38,273
That's Zip.

64
00:01:38,273 --> 00:01:39,163
He's a cat sign.

65
00:01:39,163 --> 00:01:40,523
He's also a coward.

66
00:01:40,373 --> 00:01:42,583
I'm fragile. It
says so on my box.

67
00:01:42,773 --> 00:01:44,913
Nine years ago, my
mother walked out.

68
00:01:44,913 --> 00:01:47,703
She left me her coat, and
one word in the glass.

69
00:01:47,703 --> 00:01:48,293
Wait.

70
00:01:48,343 --> 00:01:49,643
I'm done waiting.

71
00:01:50,703 --> 00:01:52,203
Mara. This is our shop.

72
00:01:52,183 --> 00:01:53,253
Backwards.

73
00:01:53,193 --> 00:01:55,183
Oh no. I look
terrible backwards.

74
00:01:55,303 --> 00:01:56,903
And then the lamp came on.

75
00:01:56,883 --> 00:01:58,353
Please tell me you did that.

76
00:01:58,473 --> 00:02:00,393
There was fresh
glass on the bench.

77
00:02:00,393 --> 00:02:01,293
Still warm.

78
00:02:01,553 --> 00:02:02,713
Don't. Don't what?

79
00:02:03,033 --> 00:02:03,963
Turn.

80
00:02:04,163 --> 00:02:04,393
Mara?

81
00:02:04,393 --> 00:02:05,993
Someone is sitting behind us.

82
00:02:06,043 --> 00:02:07,693
So of course, I turned.

83
00:02:08,493 --> 00:02:10,423
She was wearing
my mother's coat.

84
00:02:11,283 --> 00:02:13,073
There is only one
coat like this.

85
00:02:13,073 --> 00:02:14,403
And I'm wearing it.

86
00:02:14,453 --> 00:02:15,853
So is she. Awkward.

87
00:02:16,053 --> 00:02:17,023
Mom?

88
00:02:17,623 --> 00:02:18,483
That's not your mom.

89
00:02:18,483 --> 00:02:19,993
That's you, with worse hair.

90
00:02:20,193 --> 00:02:21,533
She opened her mouth.

91
00:02:21,533 --> 00:02:22,913
Nothing came out.

92
00:02:23,113 --> 00:02:24,383
So she bent glass.

93
00:02:24,383 --> 00:02:25,363
Fast, like me.

94
00:02:25,363 --> 00:02:25,573
No.

95
00:02:25,573 --> 00:02:27,003
Exactly like me.

96
00:02:27,893 --> 00:02:29,783
Crane? Our landlord,
Mister Crane?

97
00:02:29,793 --> 00:02:30,953
He raised the rent.

98
00:02:30,953 --> 00:02:32,413
He's not a monster.

99
00:02:32,413 --> 00:02:33,773
He raised it twice.

100
00:02:34,773 --> 00:02:36,873
One leaves. What does that mean?

101
00:02:37,173 --> 00:02:38,903
Mara, my tubes feel funny.

102
00:02:39,713 --> 00:02:41,743
Good evening, Miss Reyes.

103
00:02:42,143 --> 00:02:42,993
You're early.

104
00:02:42,993 --> 00:02:46,223
I wasn't going to collect
you until tomorrow.

105
00:02:46,423 --> 00:02:48,023
Get away from my cat.

106
00:02:48,123 --> 00:02:49,453
Oh, this old thing?

107
00:02:49,453 --> 00:02:51,633
I have his fuse right here.

108
00:02:51,933 --> 00:02:53,643
Mara, I'm not scared. I'm just

109
00:02:53,693 --> 00:02:54,583
Zip?
